.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
.DS_Store
*.pyc
# `python3 site_build.py`. The site SOURCE (assets, site/content/, site/data/) IS committed.
# macOS
# Pipeline runtime outputs (regenerated each run: review queue, drafts, approvals,
# published payloads). The pipeline CODE, prompts, config, and fixtures ARE committed.
# Python bytecode (CI and local runs; never commit)
# Session-local tool config
# The site deploy folder is a build artifact, fully reproducible from
out/
review/
site/publish/

# macOS/iCloud conflicted-copy artifacts ("wrap 2.py", "crypto-news-brief 2.yml").
# Every one found on 2026-09-03 was a byte-exact older revision of its real file, so
# nothing is lost by ignoring them, and a stray copy of a workflow file in
# .github/workflows/ would register as a SECOND scheduled job if it were ever committed.
* [0-9].*
* [0-9]

# S-2b (Jack, 14 October 2026): the conditions intake writes this on every build, from the
# Worker. The build publishes it at /data/conditions.json; it is never committed.
site/data/conditions.json
node_modules/
